# ── EVERY key file, whatever it is called (7 October 2026) ─────────────────
# Only ".env" itself used to be blocked. On 26 September a backup copy named
# ".env.before-migration-2026-09-25" was made during the database move, did not
# match that one exact name, and was uploaded to GitHub with the old Tokyo
# keys inside. These two lines block every ".env" file of any name, anywhere,
# and allow only the harmless sample ".env.example".
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
